{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01JPAiwTMRo4yCZdXPpWk9qa","type":"tool_result","content":"# offline replica, data as of 2026-03-01T00:00:00Z\nKAFKA-20168: Upgrade jetty to fix CVE-2025-5115\nstatus:\tResolved\nresolution:\tFixed\npriority:\tMinor\nassignee:\tMing-Yen Chung\nreporter:\tChia-Ping Tsai\nissuetype:\t(none)\ncomponents:\t(none)\nlabels:\t(none)\nfixVersions:\t4.0.2, 4.1.2, 4.3.0\ncreated:\t2026-02-11T10:31:31Z\nupdated:\t2026-02-25T11:04:33Z\npull requests:\t#21452, #21461, #21462, #21505, #21559, #21560, #21561, #21562\ncomments:\t9\n\n--- description\nfrom https://lists.apache.org/thread/y0qhof032qyxvm28yvor76w13320cfs5\n\nhttps://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2025-5115\n\n--- comment 2026-02-11T19:23:16.791000Z Matthias J. Sax\n[~chia7712] – How critical is this? Hope it's not a blocker for 4.2 release? What about 4.1.2 and 4.0.2 releases?\n\n--- comment 2026-02-12T05:59:28.025000Z Chia-Ping Tsai\nThe CVE is related to HTTP/2, and since the org.eclipse.jetty.http2 package does not appear in our codebase, we should be safe.\n\n--- comment 2026-02-12T14:25:55.002000Z Viktor Somogyi-Vass\nI'm currently in the process of making an RC release for 4.0.2. Did a CVE scan yesterday and this didn't show up. Similarly to [~chia7712] I didn't see this in our codebase. However, since I'm waiting for KAFKA-20131, I think we can merge this on 4.0.2 since it's simple. Doesn't hurt to have it and we can merge it sooner than KAFKA-20131.\n\n--- comment 2026-02-12T19:49:00.849000Z Chia-Ping Tsai\n[~viktorsomogyi] sure thing. This one is much simpler to handle, so I'll get it done before we wrap up KAFKA-20131\n\n--- comment 2026-02-12T19:50:34.485000Z Chia-Ping Tsai\nUgh, you beat me by a second! You've already merged it into 4.0. 😂\n\n--- comment 2026-02-12T20:12:34.014000Z Andrew Schofield\n[~mingyen066] Thanks for merging into 4.1 also. You saved me a job.\n\n--- comment 2026-02-12T20:36:16.734000Z Chia-Ping Tsai\ntrunk: https: